# Back away from a surface, so the robot can turn and walk off without dragging an arm across it.
#
# "Back" is a lie the gait cannot honour. g1_gait_shaper compares forward speed SIGNED, so any
# negative vx is zeroed at any magnitude, and the policy measures -0.247 m/s for a commanded
# -0.60 anyway -- reverse is entirely inside the dead zone. So this turns around, walks forward,
# and optionally faces back. See docs/notes/m9-base-approach.md.

# How far to end up from where it started, in metres. Achieved to within about one gait pulse.
float64 distance_m
# Face the original heading again at the end. A mission that is about to navigate somewhere else
# does not need it and pays two turns for nothing; a mission that wants to look at what it just
# put down does.
bool restore_heading
# Give up after this many seconds. 0 uses the server's own default.
float64 timeout_s
---
bool success
string message
float64 travelled_m
---
string PHASE_TURNING=turning
string PHASE_WALKING=walking
string PHASE_RESTORING=restoring
string phase
float64 travelled_m
